  "findings": [
    "Original Schroder305--306 defines the inverse operations and C0/C1/C2; mathematical citation matches.",
    "Original Mendelsohn Theorems1,5 match the correspondence and nontrivial existence spectrum; n=1 is independently trivial under the book definition.",
    "Original Cannon Supplement13 introduces the unrelated topological grope; the bibliographic range/year matches E038.",
    "Original Bennett full article and Stein section8 are still unavailable. Their Crossref bibliographic records are verified; metadata and indexed excerpts are not treated as full original-page verification.",
    "Caltech1968 anecdote is author testimony, not independently documented history. Priority of Schroder is not asserted."
  ]
